NAME
     nl - number lines

SYNOPSIS
     nl [-ba|-bt] [-w N] [-s STR] [FILE...]
     rev [FILE...]
     expand [-t N] [FILE...]

DESCRIPTION
     nl copies its input with a line number in front of each line.
     Called as rev it reverses each line; called as expand it turns tabs
     into spaces.

OPTIONS
     -ba     number every line
     -bt     number only the lines with something on them (the default)
     -w N    the number is N columns wide
     -s STR  put STR between the number and the line
     -t N    expand: a tab stop every N columns

SEE ALSO
     cat(1), fmt is not provided
